1,Oyda - YouTube MusicStream Pandora - Oydá (Original Mix) by Pandora Live | Listen ...Oyda language — GrokipediaOyda language resources | Joshua ProjectSinging the Individual: Name Tunes in Oyda and YopnoSinging the individual: name tunes in Oyda and Yopno,https://music.youtube.com/watch?v=XhgOkEvchLI,"Playing from Oyda Mix Autoplay Add similar content to the end of the queue Oyda Fiesta Rondalla 2:35 Autoplay is on Stream Pandora - Oydá (Original Mix) by Pandora Live on desktop and mobile. Play over 320 million tracks for free on SoundCloud. The Oyda language is classified as a member of the Omotic branch within the Afro-Asiatic language phylum, specifically belonging to the North Omotic division and the Ometo subgroup. [4] Listing of people groups speaking Oyda. Oyda dialects and alternate names. Bible and ministry resource availability. Among the Oyda of Ethiopia and the Yopno of Papua New Guinea, a distinct musical tune is closely associated with each individual. In fact, these tunes are more uniquely associated with individuals than proper names are. In their use of melodies to directly represent individual people, the Oyda and Yopno name tune systems differ from surrogate speech systems elsewhere that either: (a) mimic linguistic forms, or (b) use music to represent a relatively small set of messages.",Oyda,Afro-Asiatic
